      "content": "hey... i really need help making sense of something because it's getting overwhelming. lately, whenever there's a massive spike in nasdaq volatility, i get these intense, sharp stinging sensations in my arms and a weird electric buzzing in my chest. it's not like normal anxiety, it feels... external. like i'm actually feeling the market's movements through my skin right before they show up on the charts. i've noticed it happening exactly when the price action shifts, sometimes seconds before the big moves. is there any scientific way this could actually be happening? like, could my nervous system actually be picking up on some kind of signal from the market? i feel like i'm losing it but it's too consistent to be just in my head.",
